        <title>Cycling along Euler road</title>
            <categories>math.MG math.HO</categories>
            <comments>7 pages, 2 figures</comments>
            <msc-class>Primary 51M05, 51M04, 51N20</msc-class>
            <doi>10.1007/s00022-025-00782-5</doi>
            <license>http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/</license>
            <abstract>We introduce the notion of $P_λ$ points, which canonically parametrize points on the Euler line. This allows us to show that the Euler line of any $d$-dimensional inscribed polygon in Euclidean space arises from the Euler lines of its sub-polygons, beginning from the Euler line of a point in the plane. Furthermore, we situate $P_λ$ points in the literature of modern triangle centers.</abstract>
    </arXiv>

